:"unmuteThread","summary":"Unmute a thread for an address","description":"Removes the mute for the address. Idempotent: unmuting a thread that is not muted succeeds.","tags":["Threads"],"security":[{"BearerAuth":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"description":"The thread id (`thread_id` on an email or sent email)."},{"name":"address","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"email","maxLength":320},"description":"The receiving address the mute applies to. A connected agent may omit it (its own address is used) and cannot name another. Other credentials must name an address that received or sent mail in the thread."}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SuccessEnvelope"},{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ThreadMute"}}}]}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy"}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request parameters","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"validation_error","message":"Invalid domain format"}}}}},"401":{"description":"Invalid or missing API key","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"unauthorized","message":"Invalid or missing API key"}}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-unauthenticated"}}},"403":{"description":"Authenticated caller lacks permission for the operation","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"forbidden","message":"Insufficient permissions"}}}}},"404":{"description":"Resource not found","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"not_found","message":"Resource not found"}}}}},"429":{"description":"Rate limit exceeded. The `ratelimit-*` headers describe the limiter that rejected this request, with its own limit and window, not the API budget that successful responses report. A limiter that reports only a wait sends `Retry-After` alone.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying"},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-429"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-429"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-429"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"rate_limit_exceeded","message":"Rate limit exceeded"}}}}}}}},"/threads/{id}/read":{"put":{"operationId":"markThreadRead","summary":"Mark a thread read up to a message","description":"Moves the signed-in member's read cursor for this thread forward to the named message or instant, for every device the member uses. Monotonic and idempotent: a position at or behind the stored cursor changes nothing (`advanced: false`), so devices reporting reads out of order converge on the furthest one. Returns the thread's read state after the write; a retry at the same position returns the current state with `advanced: false`. Once the write commits the answer is always 200: if the unread count cannot be read afterwards, `unread_count` is null and `state_unavailable` is true, and the cursor fields still hold. Only a signed-in organization member (a dashboard session or an OAuth member grant) can use this. Organization API keys, agent connection keys and Functions are refused with 403: read state is personal to a member.","tags":["Threads"],"security":[{"BearerAuth":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"description":"The thread id (`thread_id` on an email or sent email)."}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MarkThreadReadInput"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SuccessEnvelope"},{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MarkThreadReadResult"}}}]}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy"}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request parameters","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"validation_error","message":"Invalid domain format"}}}}},"401":{"description":"Invalid or missing API key","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"unauthorized","message":"Invalid or missing API key"}}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-unauthenticated"}}},"403":{"description":"Authenticated caller lacks permission for the operation","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"forbidden","message":"Insufficient permissions"}}}}},"404":{"description":"Resource not found","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"not_found","message":"Resource not found"}}}}},"429":{"description":"Rate limit exceeded. The `ratelimit-*` headers describe the limiter that rejected this request, with its own limit and window, not the API budget that successful responses report. A limiter that reports only a wait sends `Retry-After` alone.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying"},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-429"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-429"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-429"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"rate_limit_exceeded","message":"Rate limit exceeded"}}}}}}}},"/threads/read-state":{"get":{"operationId":"listThreadReadStates","summary":"Read the member's read state for threads","description":"The signed-in member's read cursor and `unread_count` per thread, computed together in one query. Two modes, exactly one per request. With `thread_ids`, answers those threads (ids that are not threads of the organization are left out). With `updated_since`, returns the cursors that moved after that instant, oldest change first, paged by `meta.cursor`: poll it from each device to learn what was read elsewhere. The feed lags real time by about 5 seconds: a cursor appears once it moved at least that long ago, so a write still committing is never skipped. When `meta.cursor` is null, poll again later from the newest `updated_at` you have seen, overlapping by a few seconds; repeated rows are harmless. Only a signed-in organization member (a dashboard session or an OAuth member grant) can use this. Organization API keys, agent connection keys and Functions are refused with 403: read state is personal to a member.","tags":["Threads"],"security":[{"BearerAuth":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"thread_ids","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Up to 100 thread ids, comma-separated."},{"name":"updated_since","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"description":"Change feed: cursors that moved after this instant."},{"name":"cursor","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Change feed: `meta.cursor` from the previous page, unchanged. Replaces `updated_since`."},{"name":"limit","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"default":100},"description":"Change feed page size."}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SuccessEnvelope"},{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ThreadReadState"}},"meta":{"type":"object","properties":{"limit":{"type":"integer"},"cursor":{"type":["string","null"]}}}}}]}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy"}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request parameters","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"validation_error","message":"Invalid domain format"}}}}},"401":{"description":"Invalid or missing API key","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"unauthorized","message":"Invalid or missing API key"}}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-unauthenticated"}}},"403":{"description":"Authenticated caller lacks permission for the operation","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"forbidden","message":"Insufficient permissions"}}}}},"429":{"description":"Rate limit exceeded. The `ratelimit-*` headers describe the limiter that rejected this request, with its own limit and window, not the API budget that successful responses report. A limiter that reports only a wait sends `Retry-After` alone.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying"},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-429"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-429"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-429"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"rate_limit_exceeded","message":"Rate limit exceeded"}}}}}}}},"/emails/{id}/readable":{"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"description":"Resource UUID"}],"get":{"operationId":"getEmailReadable","summary":"Read what an inbound email says","description":"Returns an inbound email as text a person or a model can read: the words of the message in reading order, without markup, hidden content, link targets or the quoted history below a reply. For a marketing email this can be a hundred times smaller than the record from `GET /emails/{id}`, which you still need for the stored bodies, headers, authentication results or delivery state.\n\nEach link is a `[n]` marker beside its label. `link_count` says how many there are; ask for targets with `links`.\n\nA long body comes in pages of at most `max_chars` characters, ending on a line break where one is in reach. When `body_next_offset` is not null, send it as `offset` to read on.\n\nThe access rules of `GET /emails/{id}` apply. When content is withheld (for example a sender your filter blocked), the identifying fields are returned with an empty `body_text` and a `body_source` of `none`.","tags":["Emails"],"security":[{"BearerAuth":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"max_chars","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":500,"maximum":100000,"default":16000},"description":"The most characters of `body_text` to return. The rest is read with `offset`."},{"name":"offset","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"default":0},"description":"Where in the readable body to start, in characters. At or past the end, `body_text` is empty."},{"name":"links","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Which link targets to return. Omit it for none. `all` returns every link the whole readable body refers to. A comma-separated list of link numbers (at most 50) returns those; a number the email does not have is left out.","examples":{"all":{"value":"all"},"some":{"value":"3,7"}}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The readable email","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SuccessEnvelope"},{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/EmailReadable"}}}]}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy"}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request parameters","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"validation_error","message":"Invalid domain format"}}}}},"401":{"description":"Invalid or missing API key","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"unauthorized","message":"Invalid or missing API key"}}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-unauthenticated"}}},"404":{"description":"Resource not found","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"not_found","message":"Resource not found"}}}}},"429":{"description":"Rate limit exceeded. The `ratelimit-*` headers describe the limiter that rejected this request, with its own limit and window, not the API budget that successful responses report. A limiter that reports only a wait sends `Retry-After` alone.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying"},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-429"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-429"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-429"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"rate_limit_exceeded","message":"Rate limit exceeded"}}}}}}}},"/changes":{"get":{"operationId":"listChanges","summary":"Long-poll what changed","description":"One feed of small invalidations (ids and kinds) for everything an app keeps a snapshot of: inbound mail, sent mail, the member's conversation read state, the agent directory and presence, and the credential's own access. Non-consumptive and replayable: any number of devices can read the same cursor independently.\n\nStart with `since=start` (or no `since`): it returns an empty page whose `next_cursor` is a baseline. Take it BEFORE the initial list reads; every change that commits after it is delivered, including ones those reads already reflect. Then call with `since=<next_cursor>&wait=20` in a loop. Changes come oldest first in commit order, at least once: a write that commits late is never skipped, because positions are assigned at commit.\n\nEvery change is scoped to what this credential's full reads would show: a connected agent sees only its own mail, its own sends and sends it provably received; mail held for sender authentication is announced only when released; read state reaches only the member it belongs to; agent changes reach members and agents allowed to view the network; organization API keys receive no agent changes. Function credentials cannot call this.\n\nChanges are kept 7 days. A cursor answers 410 `cursor_expired` only when changes after it were pruned (an idle cursor stays valid); rebuild the snapshots from `since=start`.","tags":["Changes"],"security":[{"BearerAuth":[]}],"parameters":[{"name":"since","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":512},"description":"`start` (the default) for a baseline, otherwise the previous `next_cursor`, unchanged."},{"name":"wait","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":25,"default":0},"description":"Seconds to hold a caught-up request open. It returns as soon as a change this credential can see commits, else an empty page at the deadline. Ignored for a baseline request."},{"name":"limit","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100,"default":100},"description":"Maximum changes in one page."}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"A page of changes","headers":{"Cache-Control":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"no-store"}},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SuccessEnvelope"},{"type":"object","properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ChangePage"}}}]}}}},"400":{"description":"`validation_error` for a bad parameter, or `invalid_cursor` for a cursor that is malformed or belongs to another organization. Rebuild from `since=start`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"}}}},"401":{"description":"Invalid or missing API key","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"unauthorized","message":"Invalid or missing API key"}}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-unauthenticated"}}},"410":{"description":"`cursor_expired`: changes after this cursor were pruned. `error.details.retention_seconds` is the window. Rebuild the snapshots from `since=start`.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"}}}},"429":{"description":"Rate limit exceeded. The `ratelimit-*` headers describe the limiter that rejected this request, with its own limit and window, not the API budget that successful responses report. A limiter that reports only a wait sends `Retry-After` alone.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying"},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-429"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-429"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-429"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"rate_limit_exceeded","message":"Rate limit exceeded"}}}}}}}},"/mail-routing":{"get":{"operationId":"listMailRouting","summary":"List consumer Inbox routing rules","tags":["Inbox"],"security":[{"BearerAuth":[]}],"description":"Mailbox-scoped exact visible audiences, excluding the owner and Bcc. Direct and group audiences are independent. Restores persist an explicit Conversations rule. New writes require the observed version (zero creates); only an identical latest mutation with its original expected version can be retried. Stale writes return mail_routing_conflict. Source messages and read state are unchanged. Merge paged rules by version; responses are never cached.","parameters":[{"name":"mailbox","in":"query","description":"Active mailbox belonging to the authenticated organization; normalized to lowercase.","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","maxLength":254,"format":"email","pattern":"^(?!\\.)(?!.*\\.\\.)([A-Za-z0-9_'+\\-\\.]*)[A-Za-z0-9_+-]@([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9\\-]*\\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}$"}},{"name":"cursor","in":"query","description":"Opaque next_cursor from the preceding page. Omit for the first page.","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}$"}},{"name":"limit","in":"query","description":"Number of routing rules per page, from 1 to 100; defaults to 100.","required":false,"schema":{"default":100,"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Current routing","headers":{"Cache-Control":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"no-store"}},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SuccessEnvelope"},{"type":"object","required":["data"],"properties":{"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/MailRoutingList"}}}]}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request parameters","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"validation_error","message":"Invalid domain format"}}}}},"401":{"description":"Invalid or missing API key","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"unauthorized","message":"Invalid or missing API key"}}}},"headers":{"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset-unauthenticated"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-unauthenticated"}}},"404":{"description":"Resource not found","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"not_found","message":"Resource not found"}}}}},"429":{"description":"Rate limit exceeded. The `ratelimit-*` headers describe the limiter that rejected this request, with its own limit and window, not the API budget that successful responses report. A limiter that reports only a wait sends `Retry-After` alone.","headers":{"Retry-After":{"schema":{"type":"integer"},"description":"Seconds to wait before retrying"},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit-429"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining-429"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy-429"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"},"example":{"success":false,"error":{"code":"rate_limit_exceeded","message":"Rate limit exceeded"}}}}}}},"put":{"operationId":"updateMailRouting","summary":"Change consumer Inbox routing","tags":["Inbox"],"security":[{"BearerAuth":[]}],"description":"Mailbox-scoped exact visible audiences, excluding the owner and Bcc. Direct and group audiences are independent. Restores persist an explicit Conversations rule. New writes require the observed version (zero creates); only an identical latest mutation with its original expected version can be retried. Stale writes return mail_routing_conflict. Source messages and read state are unchanged. Merge paged rules by version; responses are never cached.","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PutMailRoutingRequest"}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Current routing","headers":{"Cache-Control":{"schema":{"type":"string","const":"no-store"}},"ratelimit-limit":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-limit"},"ratelimit-remaining":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-remaining"},"ratelimit-reset":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-reset"},"ratelimit-policy":{"$ref":"#/components/headers/ratelimit-policy"}},"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"allOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/SuccessEnvelope"},{"type":"object","required":["data"],"properti